    <properties>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <Project.name>Section-04-Exploring-Spring-Framework-Advanced-Features</Project.name>
        <start-class>com.tutorials.sid.spring.App</start-class>
    </properties>
    <!--
    what is the difference between spring-boot-starter-parent and spring-boot-starter dependency
    1.  spring-boot-starter-parent is a parent pom that provides default configurations and dependencies for Spring Boot projects.
    It includes the spring-boot-starter dependency and other commonly used dependencies.
    2.  On the other hand, spring-boot-starter is a dependency that provides a set of commonly used dependencies for a specific
    Spring Boot module or feature. By using spring-boot-starter-parent, you can inherit the default configurations
    and dependencies provided by Spring Boot, while using spring-boot-starter allows you to include only the specific dependencies
    you need for your project.
    3.  The fundamental difference is that spring-boot-starter-parent is a project management tool (a Parent POM)
    that configures your entire build environment, whereas spring-boot-starter is an actual library dependency
    that pulls core Spring Boot features into your application's classpath.

    Feature                         spring-boot-starter-parent                      spring-boot-starter
    Maven Element                   Declared in the <parent> tag.                   Declared in the <dependencies> tag.
    Primary Purpose                 Manages dependency versions,                    Serves as the fundamental "starter kit"
                                    default Java compilation levels,                to download core Spring Boot frameworks,
                                    encoding settings, and plugin                   auto-configuration engines, and logging tools.
                                    configurations.
    Quantity                        Only one parent project is                      Multiple starter dependencies
                                    allowed per Maven project.                      can be added alongside it (e.g., web, security, test)
    Classpath Impact                Does not add JAR files directly                 Directly populates your classpath
                                    to the project's runtime classpath.             with essential framework JAR files.
    -->
    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.tutorials.sid.spring</groupId>         <!-- or inherited parent groupId -->
            <artifactId>Spring-MOCK-Data-App</artifactId>
            <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>                  <!--optional if inherited from parent -->
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
